  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-3d950999-7fff-30a7-15a8-e45a523f0cc0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, as submitted, would fail to respond appropriately to the architectural and historic character of the host building and the Hoxton Street Conservation Area. It would introduce an unsympathetic contemporary appearance, while the visually prominent plant equipment would result in additional visual clutter and would not be adequately screened or integrated into the building. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Hoxton Street Conservation Area and would cause harm to the significance of the affected heritage assets, contrary to Policies LP1 (Design), LP3 (Heritage and Conservation) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, Policy HC1 of the London Plan (2021), Policies  HE5, HE6 and HE9 of the NPPF 2026, and the Commercial Extensions and Alterations SPD 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; white-space: pre-wrap; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, as submitted, fails to demonstrate that adequate measures would be secured to mitigate noise, pollution and odour arising from the proposed commercial use. The proposal has not demonstrated that neighbouring residential occupiers, particularly those located directly above the premises, would be adequately protected from noise and odour impacts. The development would therefore result in unacceptable adverse impacts on the amenity and living conditions of neighbouring residential occupiers, contrary to Policies LP2 (Development and Amenity) and LP58 (Improving the Environment – Pollution) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, Policies D13 (Agent of Change) and D14 (Noise) of the London Plan (2021) SI1 (Improving air quality), and Policy P3 of the NPPF 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ]
}